{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id308051670"}, "name":{"label":"TIberi.us"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2023-02-18T22:41:30-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"3.3.6"}, "id":{"label":"9632751972"}, "title":{"label":"Stop the scroll"}, "content":{"label":"Great app idea. Will definitely trial it and see how it works and if it helps. \n\nCould be better if the “one app for free only” was more clearly spelled out in the freemium matrix. You do say “unlimited apps” for “Pro”. But you don’t spell out how many you get for free. \n\nAlso, if you configure a second or third app, instead of the breathing exercise you get a warning that you’re missing out and need to pay for Pro to do that. So I disabled my extra automations and left one active. But I still got the “too many” warning. I then deleted the extra automations, and still I get the warning. So now the breathing exercise won’t work. Even if I delete ALL automations and add back one for my free level, the breathing exercise doesn’t come back. I just see the “you’re missing out” freemium teaser list. That’s frustrating. \n\nThis last thing seems like a bug.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=1532875441&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
